Privacy Policy for Outfitly
Last Updated: April 13, 2026

1. Introduction
Welcome to Outfitly ("we," "our," or "us"), developed by o1e3studio. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you use our mobile application Outfitly (the "App"). Please read this policy carefully. If you disagree with its terms, please stop using the App.

2. Information We Collect
2.1 Information You Provide Directly
Wardrobe Photos: When you add clothing items to your digital wardrobe, you grant the App permission to access your device's photo library or camera to capture and store these images. These photos are stored locally on your device and are never uploaded to any external server by us.
Outfit & Trip Data: Information about outfits you create, lookbooks, calendar entries, and trip plans are stored locally on your device using an on-device database (SQLite). We do not transmit this data to our servers.
App Preferences: Settings such as theme preferences (dark/light mode) and first-launch state are stored locally using Shared Preferences on your device.
2.2 Information Collected Automatically
Device & App Information
We may collect non-personally identifiable technical information to improve the App experience, including:

Device operating system and version
App version
Crash logs and error diagnostics
In-App Purchase Information (via RevenueCat)
When you subscribe to Outfitly Pro, we use RevenueCat (a third-party subscription management service) to process and manage your subscription. RevenueCat may collect:

Purchase history and subscription status
A unique anonymous user identifier
Transaction receipts (provided by Google Play)
Device type and operating system
RevenueCat does not collect your name, email address, or financial/payment card information. Payment processing is handled entirely by Google Play. You can review RevenueCat's Privacy Policy at: https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy

3. Permissions We Request
The App may request the following device permissions:

Permission	Purpose
Camera	To photograph clothing items for your digital wardrobe
Read External Storage / Photos & Media	To select existing photos of clothing from your gallery
Write External Storage	To save exported outfit images (Studio Mode) to your device gallery
Internet	Required for RevenueCat subscription management and verification
Billing (com.android.vending.BILLING)	Required by Google Play to enable in-app subscriptions
Receive Boot Completed	To reschedule local notifications after device restart
Post Notifications	To send local reminders and outfit scheduling notifications
All permissions are requested at the time they are needed and you can deny or revoke them at any time through your device settings. Denying a permission may limit some features of the App.

4. How We Use Your Information
We use the information collected to:

Provide, operate, and maintain the App and its features
Process and manage your Outfitly Pro subscription via RevenueCat and Google Play
Send local push notifications for outfit reminders you have set
Improve the App's functionality and user experience
Monitor and analyze usage patterns to fix bugs and improve performance
Comply with applicable laws and regulations
5. On-Device AI Processing (Google ML Kit)
The App uses Google ML Kit Subject Segmentation to provide the AI Background Removal feature. This processing is performed entirely on your device (on-device inference). Your clothing photos are never sent to Google's servers for this purpose. ML Kit processes images locally using the on-device model.

For more information: https://developers.google.com/ml-kit/privacy

6. Data Sharing and Disclosure
We do not sell, trade, or rent your personal information to third parties. We may share information only in the following limited circumstances:

Third-Party Service Providers
RevenueCat: For subscription status management and purchase verification. See Section 2.2.
Google Play Billing: To process in-app subscription payments. Google's Privacy Policy applies: https://policies.google.com/privacy
Legal Requirements
We may disclose your information if required to do so by law or in response to valid requests by public authorities (e.g., a court or a government agency).

7. Data Retention and Storage
Local Data: All wardrobe photos, outfit data, calendar entries, and trip plans are stored exclusively on your device. You can delete this data at any time by clearing the App's data through your device settings or by uninstalling the App.
Subscription Data: Subscription records managed by RevenueCat are retained per their data retention policies. You may request deletion of your RevenueCat data by contacting us.
We do not operate cloud servers that store your personal wardrobe or outfit data.
8. Data Security
We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect your information. Since all personal wardrobe data is stored locally on your device, the security of this data also depends on the security measures you have in place on your device (e.g., screen lock, encryption).

Subscription-related data handled by RevenueCat is protected by their industry-standard security practices.

9. Children's Privacy
The App is not directed to children under the age of 13 (or the applicable minimum age in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children. If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child has provided us with personal information, please contact us so we can take appropriate action.

10. Your Rights
Depending on your location, you may have the following rights regarding your data:

Access: Request information about what data we hold about you.
Deletion: Request deletion of your personal data. For locally stored data, you can achieve this by clearing the App's storage or uninstalling it.
Portability: Export your subscription data (handled by RevenueCat).
Opt-out of notifications: Disable push notifications through your device settings at any time.
Subscription cancellation: Cancel your Outfitly Pro subscription at any time through the Google Play subscription management page.
To exercise your rights or for any data-related requests, please contact us at: 
o1e3studio@gmail.com

11. In-App Purchases and Subscriptions
Outfitly offers an Outfitly Pro subscription purchased through Google Play In-App Billing. By subscribing:

Payment is charged to your Google Play account at confirmation of purchase.
Subscription automatically renews unless cancelled at least 24 hours before the end of the current period.
You can manage and cancel your subscription through your Google Play Account settings.
We do not have access to your payment card details. All payment information is handled by Google Play.
